From: HandSonic <8078023+handsonic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:57:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] net: airoha: fence Ethernet DMA before teardown

Stop registered netdevs and NAPI before tearing down shared PPE and QDMA
state. Keep QDMA descriptors, forwarding buffers and PPE DMA tables explicitly
owned by the driver so they are released only after the terminal reset fence
proves the hardware cannot access them.

Escalate failed PPE quiesce to the NPU hard-stop path, assert the Ethernet
reset lines before freeing shared DMA memory, and quarantine the allocations
when that fence cannot be verified.

Signed-off-by: HandSonic <8078023+handsonic@users.noreply.github.com>
